00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.143
Real mining.

00:13:15.143 --> 00:13:16.560
So the challenge with real mining

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.470
is it's very capital intensive

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.690
because you have to buy ASICs,

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.510
these specialized
semiconductors used for mining,

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.770 position:63%
or GPUs in the case of Ethereum or FPGAs

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:30.120 position:58%
in the case of zero knowledge proofs.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.100
You buy physical stuff.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.320 position:56%
And that physical stuff's expensive.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:35.670
And when you raise capital,

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.200
and in particular venture capital,

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.840
people don't necessarily
wanna give you money

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.030 position:63%
to buy a bunch of depreciating hardware.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.590
So you finance it.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.200
There's a lot of specialized
lenders in the industry

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:50.940
who specialize in lending using
the actual chips themselves

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:51.870
as the collateral.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.060 position:58%
So if I wanna borrow say $500 million

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.810
to build a new data center
